course: dictionary
lesson: 8408
title: Rumpus: a noisy fuss
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rumpus is a noisy fuss, a quarrel or a commotion. It is an informal word, so you will hear it in chatty talk and in stories more than in formal writing. Context helps you find its meaning: «Toad causes a terrible rumpus wherever he goes» tells you that a rumpus is something loud and messy that Toad makes.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Swap in "noisy fuss": "Toad causes a terrible noisy fuss wherever he goes" still makes sense, so the meaning fits. Look for clue words such as terrible, wherever and loud to help you.
explain: Rumpus has a second meaning in Australia and New Zealand, where a «rumpus room» is a family playroom. Here the word names a place, not a noise. The word room next to it shows which meaning is meant.
fact: A rumpus is a noisy fuss, quarrel or commotion.
fact: Rumpus is informal, so it is used in everyday speech and in stories.
fact: «Toad causes a terrible rumpus wherever he goes.» Toad makes a lot of noise and trouble.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, a «rumpus room» is a family playroom.
fact: The plural of rumpus is rumpuses.
exercise: «Toad causes a terrible rumpus wherever he goes.» What is a rumpus here? | A quiet nap | A long journey | *A noisy fuss | A tasty meal
exercise: The Queen of Hearts' croquet game is a rumpus. What does rumpus mean in this sentence? | A family playroom | A sleepy afternoon | A quiet game of cards | *A wild, noisy commotion
exercise: In Australia, a «rumpus room» is where the family plays. What is a rumpus room? | A kitchen with a big table | A garden shed | *A family playroom | A noisy quarrel
test: Which word is closest in meaning to rumpus? | Tidiness | Peace | *Commotion | Silence
test: «The rumpus room was full of toys and games.» What is a rumpus room? | A noisy train | *A family playroom | A shop that sells toys | A place to sleep
exam: Which sentence uses rumpus correctly? | *Her brothers made a rumpus over who would get the last biscuit | The rumpus of the sleepy cat was a gentle purr | Rumpus is a kind of bird that sings at dawn | She ate a rumpus for her lunch
